  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - In light of the numerous conflicts with Development Plan policies, the proposal would fail to comply with Local Plan policy SC1 as it proposes the formation of a self-contained residential unit within the curtilage of existing dwellings while conflicting with other policies. ",
    "Reason : 2 - Owing to its excessive scale and bulk, inappropriate siting and design, failure to preserve the established visual symmetry between no.2 and its neighbour no.63 Burns Way and spacious character of the area, and its awkward relationship with the host property and the street character, the proposal would cause significant harm to the character and appearance of the area. It would also disrupt the pattern of development along the street and would represent an overdevelopment of the site. The proposal would therefore conflict with Local Plan policies CC1 and CC2. ",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed development, as a result of the unacceptable loss of usable rear garden space to the existing dwelling at no.2 Browning Way, would result in significant harm to neighbouring living conditions, contrary to Local Plan policies CC2 and SC5",
    "Reason : 4 - The proposed development would fail to provide external amenity space of an adequate quality and quantity for future occupants. As such the application would be contrary to Local Plan policy SC5.",
    "Reason : 5 - The development has failed to demonstrate that energy consumption and carbon emission reductions have been maximised onsite as far as possible through use of viable sustainability proposals, and has also failed to include a planning obligation to secure any necessary contributions to the Council's Carbon Offset Fund to mitigate any shortfall in emission reductions. The proposal would therefore be contrary to London Plan policies SI2 and SI15, Local Plan policies EQ1 and EQ2 and IMP3 and the intent of the Council's Planning Obligations and CIL SPD and National Planning Policy Framework."
  ],
